  - THE CLOSE-CONTRADICTION CHECK ALSO PAIRS A GIVEN-UP QUOTED PHRASE WITH ITS RETURN IN THE CLOSE (pkgCQL rev 2, ASK 293; Close Enforcer Build):
    - Why: in run 37113 the defender granted in [CR2] "'Of whom was born' does not by itself remove a husband. I do not rest the exclusion on that clause." and closed in [CR4] "Matthew 1:16 gives the birth to Mary alone, by 'of whom'". No E-CLOSECON row covered LINK 1. pkgWVR pairs withdrawn verses only, and by its rule leaves out a verse named only as the place of a phrase.
    - What it does: a fourth candidate maker, cecQph, runs after pkgWVR. An earlier line in that side's round 2 or 3 that gives up a quoted phrase ("<quote> does not by itself ...", "I do not rest / no longer rest / drop / withdraw / give up ... <quote>") is paired with a closing sentence of the same side that quotes the same phrase and asserts with it (alone, only, solely, removes, excludes, gives, assigns, withholds, no human/man/father/husband). A give-up with no quote of its own takes the quotes of the sentence before it, but never from a NARROWED TO or KEPT line. The given-up phrase and the shared phrase must each hold one word that is not a small word. Questions, conditions before the verb, lines that name the opponent, ANSWER lines, closing sentences that quote 8 or more words and closing sentences that give ground are left out. At most 2 closing sentences per earlier line and 4 pairs per side. The prompt, the call, the two-check rule (pkgTWC) and the record are unchanged.
    - Size: Close Enforcer Build 28,194 to 33,524.
    - Shown offline: over 62 stored debates, candidates 123 to 131, the old candidates kept as the prefix in 62 of 62; 37113 gains the two LINK 1 pairs above.
    - Limits: an unquoted give-up ("I do not rest D1 on the feminine relative") is not paired; each new candidate is one more line in the two E-CLOSECON prompts per side (no new call). Not shown by a run.
  - A KEYSTONE CANNOT STAND ON A LINK THAT BROKE (pkgKRB rev 2, ASK 294; Shared Library LIB 1326 in cureRecompute, LIB 1608, and the own lines of Cure Check and Panel Cure Check):
    - Why: in run 37113 all three judges wrote "KEYSTONE: D7 -- STANDS". The defender's own [CR2] says "D7 rests on D2 and D3", and D2 broke by a confirmed close contradiction. (The LINK 7 close contradiction was NOT CONFIRMED, one check of two, row 38676.)
