  - A DEFENDER LINK THAT RESTS ON THE GENNAO CLAIM OR A 1:35 GROUND OF THE TITLE CANNOT STAND (pkgKDG rev 4e, ASK 304; Shared Library kagLines2024, before the ANSWER CHECK loop):
    - Why: in run 37113 all three judges graded D3 UNDERDETERMINED, though D3 reads "Dio kai (therefore also) ties the title to ... the Holy Ghost coming and the power overshadowing". DG-18: "Son of God" is a covenant title, and "therefore also" ties Luke 1:35 back to 1:32, "the Lord God shall give unto him the throne of his father David". D2 and D7 rest on "gennao ... the source named is the Holy Ghost" (Matthew 1:20), against DG-8 F2 (Wall 6444, 6445).
    - What it does: the defender's rounds cr1 to cr4 are split at link headings; long quotes (25 characters or more) and sentences reporting the other side are left out; for this check a bracket marker such as [L2] is a sentence break. A link is flagged when one of its blocks has (a) the gennao claim (the F2 forms above), or (b), in a block that names Luke 1:32 or 1:35, a DG-18 ground: a grounding term ("grounds", "ground of", "rests", "ties", "because", "therefore ... title") with the title or calling as the thing grounded and, as its ground, (i) coming, overshadowing, begetting, begotten, conception, "no human father" or "the Spirit" (capital S, never "the spirit of holiness") in the same sentence; (ii) a back-reference (that/this cause, act, clause, coming, antecedent, work) whose cause stands up to two sentences before in the same line or bullet, skipping sentences that report the other side; or (iii) the split form, 1:32 with the throne or descent and 1:35 with the ground of the title, unless the 1:35 part names the throne, David, the covenant or 1:32. A stated tie to 1:32 is null unless it is the split form; a bare "So" is not a back-reference; a negation in the sentence skips it (Wall 6497, 6510, 6513, 6516, 6519). A judge line "Dk vs Cj: STANDS / UNDERDETERMINED" or "Dk: STANDS / UNDERDETERMINED" on a flagged link is a K-AG TRIAL item, doc DG-18, carrying the ground's sentence (both when the link rests on both); it is cured only by that line written as DEFENDER LINK BROKEN (the only defender broken form in COL_GRADE). NOT HELD, and BROKEN on another pair, do not cure it.
    - Size: Shared Library 940,856 to 956,907 with pkgKDA rev 3, 14 users.
    - Shown offline: 37113 flags D2, D3, D5 and D7 (LINK 5 [CR2] "dio kai ties the title to the conception"), 37032 flags D1 and D3; doctrine items with pkgKDA, 37113 8/9/7 and 37032 3/4/2; over 62 stored debates 113 flagged links (rev 2: 87), 0 bad across all near-miss cases.
    - Limits: TRIAL (a judge who leaves the line keeps the seat; LIVE is the operator's call); the live check reads the judge's first reply, which may grade more lines than the stored final reasoning; claims in round 1 under numbered section headings are not tied to a link; a link stays flagged after the defender drops the claim; the flag rate is high (53 of 62 debates in rev 2's screen), one more cure prompt line each. Not shown by a run.
